# BUT HfGlobal still 1066 vs cjxl 670 (+396B, -56B vs WITH W44-29).
# Conclusion: W44-29 explains the strategy-distribution shift but NOT the byte wedge.
#
# === Root divergence found (HfGlobal +452B) ===
#
# Block context map (`num_block_clusters`):
#   - ours: 4 clusters (BlockCtxMap::default() = NUM_BLOCK_CTXS = 4)
#   - cjxl: 15 clusters (libjxl simple-default hardcoded map at lf.rs:69-75)
#
# Bitstream-level encoding:
#   - ours: writes bit_0 = 0 (non-default), then 16 zero bits, then encoded
#           39-entry context map with 4-cluster values via prefix code.
#           Path: bitstream.rs:999 → context_tree::write_block_context_map.
#   - cjxl: writes bit_0 = 1 (libjxl's "is_simple_block_ctx_map"=true).
#           Decoder synthesizes the hardcoded 15-cluster map at jxl-oxide/lf.rs:69-75.
#
# HfGlobal size scales with `num_contexts = 495 × num_hf_presets × num_block_clusters`.
#   - ours: 495 × 1 × 4 = 1980 → clustered to 17 ANS histograms → 5584 bits entropy code
#   - cjxl: 495 × 1 × 15 = 7425 → finer clustering opportunity → can produce tighter histograms
#
# IRONY: more contexts gives cjxl MORE flexibility to cluster (pair-merge ANS histogram
# clustering produces tighter context-specific distributions). Our 4-cluster default
# collapses too many cells into one histogram → wider per-symbol distributions →
# more bits per AC coefficient symbol → larger HfCoeff (+1345B across 4 groups).
#
# Net wedge mechanism:
#   - LfGlobal: ours saves ~36B by writing a simpler context map
#   - BUT in HfGlobal: ours pays +452B (more bits per histogram with too-wide dists)
#   - AND in HfCoeff: ours pays +1345B (4-cluster blunt entropy model can't track AC
#     distributions as tightly as 15-cluster fine-grained model)
#   - HfMetadata: ours saves -1121B (10 fewer varblocks, larger transforms)
#   - Net: +642B (the F-D wedge)
#
# === Why prior "structural ceiling" audits missed this ===
# - W44-58/59 audit looked at AFV evaluation cost-inputs (joined on strategy+x+y);
#   found them at parity. Did NOT look at LfGlobal encoding choices.
# - W44-60/61 audit looked at strategy CALL FREQUENCY; found DCT64X32 gap, fixed it.
#   Did NOT look at the post-strategy entropy coding model selection.
# - W44-33 declared "structurally unfixable" based on 6 audits but every audit was
#   in the AC strategy / cost model layer, never the block context map layer.
# - W44-39 looked at "block context map count vs cjxl" but ended in honest-stop
#   without trying the simple-default flag bit toggle.
#
# === Recommended W44-70 fix ===
#
# Hypothesis: writing `bit_0 = 1` ("simple-default") emits the libjxl-15-cluster map
# without the per-block tokenization context-map overhead, AND gives the entropy
# coder more contexts to cluster, which produces tighter ANS distributions
# and shrinks both HfGlobal (-452B saved) and HfCoeff (-1345B saved) on this
# cell. Estimated savings: ~1800B on this cell, ~9% file size win.
#
# Note: this would REQUIRE changing our encoder's COMPACT_BLOCK_CONTEXT_MAP
# entries to the libjxl 15-cluster default values (lf.rs:69-75 of jxl-oxide
# is the verbatim reference). The mapping is from (channel, order_id) →
# block_ctx ID, with 13 order_ids × 3 channels = 39 cells. libjxl's default:
#   [0, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 4, 5, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 7, 8, 9, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14, 7, 8, 9, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14]
#
# Side-effects to consider:
# - The decoder will see 15 distinct block contexts instead of 4.
# - HfCoeff context_offset arithmetic must use num_block_clusters=15.
# - Tests that hash-lock on bitstream bytes will need rebaseline (many).
# - ANS histogram count will change; per-context HybridUint configs will change.
# - Other photo cells (especially 1531677, 1189261, codec_wiki) should see similar wins.
#
